.* QHDBGCMD: command help. Generated by `cargo run -p helpaudit -- gen` from the
.* definitions and command/sys-cpps/help/; do not edit.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDBKP.Add Breakpoint (ADDBKP)
:P.Use the Add Breakpoint (ADDBKP) command to add a breakpoint at
statements of a program under debug.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/STMT'.Statement identifier (STMT)
:P.The statement identifier for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/PGMVAR'.Program variable (PGMVAR)
:P.The program variable for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Variable
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Basing pointer
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/START'.Start position (START)
:P.The start position for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/LEN'.Length (LEN)
:P.The length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DCL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/OUTFMT'.Output format (OUTFMT)
:P.The format of the output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DFTPGM.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/SKIP'.Skip count (SKIP)
:P.The skip count for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDBKP/BKPCOND'.Breakpoint condition (BKPCOND)
:P.The breakpoint condition for this command.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Variable
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Relational operator
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*EQ:EPK.
:PD.Equal to.
:PT.:PK.*NE:EPK.
:PD.Not equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GT:EPK.
:PD.Greater than.
:PT.:PK.*LT:EPK.
:PD.Less than.
:PT.:PK.*GE:EPK.
:PD.Greater than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*LE:EPK.
:PD.Less than or equal to.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGDBG.Change Debug (CHGDBG)
:P.Use the Change Debug (CHGDBG) command to change the debug attributes
of the job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDBG/MAXTRC'.Max trace statements (MAXTRC)
:P.The max trace statements for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDBG/TRCFULL'.Trace full (TRCFULL)
:P.The trace full for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*STOPTRC:EPK.
:PD.When full, the trace stops.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDBG/UPDPROD'.Update production files (UPDPROD)
:P.The update production files for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDBG/OPMSRC'.OPM source level debug (OPMSRC)
:P.The OPM source level debug for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPBKP.Display Breakpoints (DSPBKP)
:P.Use the Display Breakpoints (DSPBKP) command to show the breakpoints
set in the programs under debug.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPBKP/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPMODSRC.Display Module Source (DSPMODSRC)
:P.Use the Display Module Source (DSPMODSRC) command to open the source
debugger display for the modules under debug.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDDBG.End Debug (ENDDBG)
:P.Use the End Debug (ENDDBG) command to take the job out of debug mode.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDSRVJOB.End Service Job (ENDSRVJOB)
:P.Use the End Service Job (ENDSRVJOB) command to stop servicing the job
STRSRVJOB named.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVBKP.Remove Breakpoint (RMVBKP)
:P.Use the Remove Breakpoint (RMVBKP) command to remove breakpoints from
a program under debug.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVBKP/STMT'.Statement identifier (STMT)
:P.The statement identifier for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVBKP/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DFTPGM.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRDBG.Start Debug (STRDBG)
:P.Use the Start Debug (STRDBG) command to put the job in debug mode
with programs and service programs under debug.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/DFTPGM'.Default program (DFTPGM)
:P.The default program for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/MAXTRC'.Max trace statements (MAXTRC)
:P.The max trace statements for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 200 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/TRCFULL'.Trace full (TRCFULL)
:P.The trace full for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STOPTRC:EPK.
:PD.When full, the trace stops.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/UPDPROD'.Update production files (UPDPROD)
:P.Whether to update production files.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/OPMSRC'.OPM source level debug (OPMSRC)
:P.Whether to OPM source level debug.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/SRVPGM'.Service program (SRVPGM)
:P.The service program, by name and library.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/CLS'.Class file (CLS)
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRDBG/DSPMODSRC'.Display module source (DSPMODSRC)
:P.The display module source for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PGMDEP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRSRVJOB.Start Service Job (STRSRVJOB)
:P.Use the Start Service Job (STRSRVJOB) command to service another
job&colon. debug its programs from this one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSRVJOB/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRSRVJOB/DUPJOBOPT'.Duplicate job option (DUPJOBOPT)
:P.What happens when more than one job matches the name given&colon.
show a list to choose from, or send a message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
